intro="Everything — living beings and a house alike — is made of atoms, yet the atom itself is not the end of the story. This chapter follows the **history of atomic models** (Kanada and Democritus → Dalton → Thomson → Rutherford → Bohr), the discovery of the **electron, proton and neutron**, and then the language used to describe atoms: **symbols, atomic number, mass number, electronic configuration, valency, isotopes and isobars**.",
