("ul", ["**Homi J. Bhabha** founded TIFR and BARC and is called the father of the Indian nuclear programme. Electron microscopes (STM, TEM) let us image surfaces and arrangements of atoms."]),

("qa", [
 ("Describe Rutherford’s gold foil experiment and its conclusions.", "α-particles on thin gold foil: most passed straight, some deflected, few bounced back, showing mostly empty space and a small, dense, positive nucleus."),
 ("List the limitations of Thomson’s and Rutherford’s models.", "Thomson’s could not explain large-angle scattering; Rutherford’s could not explain why accelerating electrons do not spiral into the nucleus."),
 ("State the postulates of Bohr’s model.", "Electrons revolve in fixed shells (stationary states) with definite energies, do not radiate energy there, and change shell only by absorbing/emitting an energy equal to the difference."),
 ("Who discovered the electron, proton and neutron?", "Thomson (1897), Rutherford, Chadwick (1932)."),
 ("Define atomic number and mass number. How are they related to protons and neutrons?", "Z = number of protons; A = protons + neutrons."),
 ("State the 2n² rule and the maximum electrons in K, L, M shells.", "Maximum in nth shell = 2n²; 2, 8, 18; outermost shell not more than 8."),
 ("What is valency? Find valency of Na, O, C.", "Electrons lost, gained or shared to get a stable configuration; Na 1, O 2, C 4."),
 ("Define isotopes and give two uses.", "Same Z, different A; cobalt-60 in cancer therapy, carbon-14 in dating."),
 ("Why do isotopes of an element have similar chemical properties?", "They have the same electron number and configuration."),
 ("How do isobars differ from isotopes?", "Isobars: different elements, same mass number (e.g. Ar-40, K-40, Ca-40); isotopes: same element, different mass number."),
 ("Calculate the average atomic mass of chlorine.", "35 × 3/4 + 37 × 1/4 = 35.5 u."),
 ("Why are atoms electrically neutral?", "Number of protons (+) equals number of electrons (−).")]),
